   135	
   136	## 3. Chat Mode — proposed shape
   137	
   138	### 3.1 Mode posture
   139	
   140	Chat Mode is the user-driven, conversational orchestration mode. **The user types one task at a time; the manager runs a full per-task workflow slice and returns to the user.** No upfront task list. No autonomous multi-task runway. The session's shape is the union of all per-task slices the user types between session start and the user's explicit end-of-session signal.
   141	
   142	**Term lock — "per-task slice."** From this point in the document forward, the single canonical term for the unit Chat dispatches is **per-task slice** (synonym drift in iter1 — "per-user-typed-task slice", "task slice", "Chat task" — is resolved per Finding F-A1 / codex-aes-3d91be4a; downstream prose in `chat-mode.md` inherits this term).
   143	
   144	This re-frames the 6-step state machine. Configuration runs once at session start (unchanged). Wrap-up runs once at session end (triggered only on explicit user signal). Between them, the manager runs **per-task slices**, not linear Ideation → Preparation → Planning → Execution → Wrap-up. Each slice contains its own Ideation, its own Preparation (which resolves to `state: Skipped` at loop entry per R1), its own mini Planning, its own mini Execution, and its own task-record boundary.
   145	
   146	This is the structural change that supersedes the SKILL.md 241–242 lock. Mode no longer just controls **whether** the manager pauses for `AskUserQuestion`; mode now controls **which state machine** runs between Configuration and Wrap-up.
   147	
   148	### 3.2 Per-task slice workflow shape (diagram)
   149	
   150	```
   151	Step 1 — Configuration (once per session)
   152	   │
   153	   ▼
   154	┌──────── Per-task slice ───────────────────────────────────────────┐
   155	│  user types a task                                                 │
   156	│   │                                                                │
   157	│   ▼                                                                │
   158	│  Step 2 — Full Ideation Loop  (maxIter=2)                          │
   159	│      DISCUSSION (forced user-driven, regardless of discuss.mode)   │
   160	│           ↓                                                        │
   161	│      WORK     (leader; full 4 sub-steps A–D)                       │
   162	│           ↓                                                        │
   163	│      EVALUATION (always)                                           │
   164	│           ↓                                                        │
   165	│      MEMORIZATION  — Chat narrowed PASS path (see §3.3 canonical)  │
   166	│           ↓                                                        │
   167	│      ITER / EXIT (PASS → next; REVISE → back to DISCUSSION)        │
   168	│   │                                                                │
   169	│   ▼                                                                │
   170	│  Step 3 — Preparation Loop  ⊘  state: Skipped at loop entry        │
   171	│      (R1: settings.workflow.preparation.maxIterations: 0           │
   172	│       → manager skips DISCUSSION+WORK+EVAL+MEMO rows entirely;     │
   173	│       stamps state: Skipped; no audit-trail noise; persists        │
   174	│       workflow.chat.tasks[i].preparation = {state: "Skipped",      │
   175	│       iterations: []}.)                                            │
   176	│      The user MAY opt in for a complex task by typing an explicit  │
   177	│      prep override; opt-in runs the standard contract.             │
