   258	### 3.6 Wrap-up trigger (explicit end-of-session)
   259	
   260	In Chat Mode, Wrap-up runs **only when the user explicitly signals end-of-session**. The signal is one of:
   261	
   262	- The user selects "Wrap up the session" at the per-task user review gate.
   263	- The user types an explicit end-of-session message (e.g., "we're done", "wrap up", "end session").
   264	- The user invokes `/gobbi wrap-up` (if and when such a command exists; otherwise the message form above).
   265	
   266	The manager does NOT auto-trigger Wrap-up on any other signal (no auto-trigger on "no more tasks for now", no auto-trigger on idle, no auto-trigger after N tasks). The discipline is symmetric to the Always-Ask Destructive category: ending the session changes durable memory (mistake promotion, archive moves, handoff write) — that decision is the user's.
   267	
   268	If the user closes the session without an explicit Wrap-up signal (terminal hang-up), the partial session-memory survives (every loop's MEMORIZATION ran, transcript + session.json + artifacts all written), and a future session can resume per the existing 3-state worktree idempotency guard (`orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1` row 5).
