   415	### 6.7 § Workflow Metadata update — `workflow.chat.tasks[]` schema (R2 + R3 lock)
   416	
   417	**Additive change** to `§ Workflow Metadata` (line 426+) and `§ State persistence` (line 343+). The existing `workflow.{loop}` shape stays unchanged for Auto. A new `workflow.chat.tasks[]` field is added for Chat sessions.
   418	
   419	**Schema (both `session.json` and `state.json`):**
   420	
   421	```yaml
   422	workflow:
   423	  configuration: { ... }       # unchanged
   424	  ideation:        { ... }     # used by Auto only; Chat populates within tasks[]
   425	  preparation:     { ... }     # used by Auto only; Chat populates within tasks[]
   426	  planning:        { ... }     # used by Auto only; Chat populates within tasks[]
   427	  execution:       { ... }     # used by Auto only; Chat populates within tasks[]
   428	  wrap-up:         { ... }     # used by both modes (session-level)
   429	  chat:                         # NEW — populated only when settings.mode == "chat"
   430	    tasks:
   431	      - taskNo: 01              # zero-padded ordinal within session
   432	        slug: chat-mode-redesign-idea-doc   # subject-descriptive kebab-case
   433	        startedAt: ISO-8601
   434	        finishedAt: ISO-8601 | null
   435	        ideation:    { state, verdict, iter, maxIterations, phase, iterations[] }
   436	        preparation: { state: "Skipped", iterations: [] }    # R1 default
   437	        planning:    { state, verdict, iter, maxIterations, phase, iterations[] }
   438	        execution:   { state, verdict, iter, maxIterations, phase, iterations[] }
   439	        taskRecord:  { path, writtenAt }    # pointer to task-record.md
   440	      - taskNo: 02 ...
   441	```
   442	
   443	Notes:
   444	
   445	- The per-task `{ideation, preparation, planning, execution}` sub-records carry the same shape as the existing top-level `workflow.{loop}` entries — same `state` / `verdict` / `iter` / `maxIterations` / `phase` / `iterations[]` fields. Existing readers parse the same per-loop record shape; only the path changes (`workflow.chat.tasks[i].ideation` vs `workflow.ideation`).
   446	- `state.json.workflow.chat.tasks[]` and `session.json.workflow.chat.tasks[]` are mirrored — the `state.json` shape is the live state-machine projection (R3); the `session.json` shape archives the final iter + verdict + tokensUsed per slice (R2).
   447	- The `Workflow Status Display` (§6.3) consumes `state.json.workflow.chat.tasks[currentIndex]` for the per-task tier.
   448	- **Templates updated:** `templates/state.template.json` and `templates/session.template.json` both gain the empty `workflow.chat: { tasks: [] }` field. Both Chat and Auto sessions ship the same templates; an Auto session leaves `workflow.chat.tasks: []` empty. Addressed Codex codex-struct-6f11d0e9 (Medium) — the CRUD §7.3 now enumerates template updates.
   449	
   450	The schema is additive — no existing field changes shape. An Auto-mode reader sees the existing `workflow.{loop}` shape; a Chat-mode reader sees both (and uses `chat.tasks[]`).
