/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:52:| `assistant` | [`templates/assistant.md`](templates/assistant.md) | Narrow read-only support (lookups, references, codebase exploration). Can parallelize. |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:56:**Cross-pollination mechanism:** the v0.4.x dual-stance design (innovative + best stances as orthogonal hypothesis generators) was retired in v0.5.0 in favor of a single leader per dispatch. Orthogonal hypothesis generation is now provided by **dual-system evaluation** — Claude and Codex independently judge the leader's output, and divergence between systems is the anti-groupthink signal. See `orchestration/workflow/evaluation.md` § Why dual-system is mandatory.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:66:3. **Context** — manager-authored scene-setting (where it fits, dependencies, user-clarified intent, pre-resolved decisions).
