/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:79:- `assistant` adds **Expected Output Shape**.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:105:**No inheritance.** Even if the manager already loaded `principles` minutes earlier, every fresh subagent must load it again. There is no session inheritance.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:107:**MEMORIZATION hard gate.** When the delegated phase is MEMORIZATION (or includes a MEMORIZATION sub-phase), `memorization/SKILL.md` MUST appear in tier 3 (Skills). The memorization skill defines the memory-tier access matrix, staging rules, idempotency contract, and exit checklist that the sub-phase agent must follow. Omitting it produces an agent that cannot operate the sub-phase correctly. Per-role templates for `assistant`, `leader`, and `executor` include a placeholder for this entry; see the templates in [`templates/`](templates/).
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:109:**Project-memory standard gate.** Any delegation that **writes or evaluates project memory** MUST load `memorization/rules.md` in tier 3 (Skills) alongside `memorization/SKILL.md`. `memorization/rules.md` is the naming / frontmatter / structure standard — the rules a memory file's name, frontmatter, and scope must obey; without it the standard is advisory-only and structural drift recurs. The `leader`, `executor`, and `assistant` templates carry the `memorization/rules.md` line right after their `memorization/SKILL.md` line; the `evaluator` template carries it in tier 3 for delegations that judge project-memory artifacts against the standard (the evaluator has no `memorization/SKILL.md` line).
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:119:Every subagent's final response MUST begin with these structured lines — the **first** lines of the response body. The manager parses from the top and dispatches deterministically:
