/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:156:  description: "The executor brief cites `sessions/.../ideation/artifacts/scope-contract.md`
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:168:When a subagent emits `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` and the missing context requires user input, the response body MUST include a `user-question:` block. The manager reads this block and constructs an AskUserQuestion call on behalf of the subagent.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:182:If the missing context can be fetched without user input (e.g., by reading a file, running a command, or delegating to an assistant), the manager does that first — only escalate to the user if the manager cannot resolve it independently. The `user-question:` block signals "user input required"; absence of the block signals "manager can resolve".
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:192:| `leader` | `DONE` / `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` / `NEEDS_CONTEXT` / `BLOCKED` | — (omit VERDICT line) |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:193:| `executor` | `DONE` / `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` / `NEEDS_CONTEXT` / `BLOCKED` | — (omit VERDICT line) |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:194:| `evaluator` | `DONE` / `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` / `NEEDS_CONTEXT` / `BLOCKED` | `PASS` / `REVISE` / `FAIL` |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:195:| `assistant` | `DONE` / `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` / `NEEDS_CONTEXT` / `BLOCKED` | — (omit VERDICT line) |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:203:| `NEEDS_CONTEXT` | If `user-question:` block present: construct AskUserQuestion and ask user. Otherwise: fetch missing context (file read / assistant delegation) and re-delegate. Do NOT retry with the same prompt unchanged. |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:207:The manager translates this into its own user-facing status (`PROCEED` / `PROCEED_WITH_CONCERNS` / `NEEDS_DECISION` / `BLOCKED`) in the next user message.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:221:| `Your phase:` | `ideation` \| `preparation` \| `planning` \| `execution` \| `wrap-up` (evaluator suffixes `-eval`; research uses `research`) | yes | Routes the entry into `session.json.agents[].phase` and the matching workflow step. |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:223:| `Your sub-step:` | slug or letter (e.g., `evaluation-claude`, `A`, `B`, `claude-iter1-clean-1of3`) | when more than one spawn shares the same `(step, phase, iter)` | Disambiguates parallel spawns in the same iteration (e.g., dual-system evaluators, batched executors). |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:226:These four headers are the **only** machine-readable contract between the delegation prompt and the hook. Everything else in the prompt (Identity line, Task Description, Context, Load Directives, etc.) is for the subagent. Per-role templates ship the headers pre-filled with `<<slot>>` markers; the manager fills them at dispatch time as part of the same template-filling pass that resolves every other slot. Omitting the headers does not break the subagent, but it leaves `session.json.agents[]` entries with `phase` / `iter` / `sub-step` set to `null`, which downstream session-memory queries treat as missing data.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:230:Both the hook (`post-tool-use-agents.sh`) and its verify-and-fix companion ([`.claude/scripts/reconstruct-agents.sh`](../../../../.claude/scripts/reconstruct-agents.sh)) wrap their `session.json` read-modify-write in a POSIX `flock -x` exclusive lock (held on a sidecar `.lock` file co-located with `session.json`), then commit the new contents via `mv` for atomic replacement. The lock is the design-decision D-3-5 serialization gate: concurrent subagent spawns (e.g., the two parallel evaluators, or a research fan-out) fire PostToolUse events that arrive interleaved, and the lock guarantees the upserts apply in sequence rather than racing each other into a torn write. The manager does not need to throttle spawns or stagger dispatches; the lock makes `agents[]` writes safe under arbitrary spawn concurrency.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:236:The manager must NOT produce delegation prompts that look like these. Each is a known failure mode.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:242:- ❌ **Spec by `@path`** — "See the plan in `plans/foo.md` and implement it." Adds inference between spec and work; subagents may read it partially or interpret it differently than the manager intended. Paste the spec inline.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:244:- ❌ **No status contract** — Prompt ends mid-instruction with no `## Report Format` section. The subagent produces a prose summary the manager has to interpret.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:245:- ❌ **Author transcript leaked to evaluator** — Evaluator receives the producer's chain of thought, breaking Principle 2. Evaluators get a constructed context bundle only.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:246:- ❌ **Parallel implementation** — Spawning two executors against the same scope or against overlapping files. Implementation is sequential; only research, investigation, and evaluation parallelize.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:247:- ❌ **Per-perspective evaluator spawning** — Spawning one evaluator agent per perspective (8 agents for 7 perspectives + Overall). The canonical topology is 2 agents in parallel — one per system (Claude + Codex). Each handles all 7 perspectives + Overall sequentially per the 4-stage procedure in `evaluation/SKILL.md`. Perspective isolation is maintained within the agent's own context discipline, not by spawning separate agents per perspective.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:251:## Inline-Paste Rule
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:259:- May interpret a section out of context (without the manager's framing).
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:260:- Cannot be diffed at the dispatch level — the manager cannot see what the subagent actually received.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:268:Every evaluator delegation prompt opens with a `CRITICAL: Do Not Trust the Report` block. The evaluator is told explicitly:
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:274:Boilerplate lives in [`templates/evaluator.md`](templates/evaluator.md). The block is mandatory; do not paraphrase it.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:278:## Model Selection
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:282:Opus is reserved for roles where the quality bar depends on judgment, ambiguity-handling, and adversarial reasoning — manager (user-facing decisions), leader (open-ended investigation and decomposition), evaluator (catching non-obvious gaps an author missed). Sonnet handles roles where the work is structured against an explicit contract — executor (implements the plan within scope) and assistant (returns the asked answer with cited evidence). The manager sets `model:` on the `Agent` tool call at dispatch time — it overrides the agent definition's default.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:286:| `manager` | — | opus | Session main agent; orchestration + user discussion require deep reasoning |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:287:| `leader` | — | opus | Deep reasoning across investigation, research, and decomposition |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:288:| `executor` | — | sonnet | Implementation follows the contract; structured execution against an explicit spec |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:289:| `evaluator` | — | opus | Adversarial assessment of artifacts + process docs needs deep reasoning to catch non-obvious gaps |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:290:| `assistant` | — | sonnet | Narrow, fast support work — lookups, references, factual answers |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:294:If a specific task calls for a model different from the role's default — a particularly narrow executor task that warrants opus, or a routine evaluator check that fits sonnet — the manager sets `model:` on the `Agent` call explicitly and documents the reason in the delegation prompt's `## Context` block. The role's default is the right choice unless the manager can articulate why this task is exceptional.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:302:**Specificity vs autonomy** — Over-specified prompts produce rigid work; under-specified prompts miss requirements. Templates give a deterministic floor; the manager calibrates the slot content based on how well-defined the task is.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:312:**When to specify verification commands** — Always for executors. Manager specifies the exact `bun test` / `bun run check` / etc. commands in the `## Verification Commands` block. The executor runs them and pastes the output; manager parses for `DONE` vs `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS`.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:320:The manager delegates to these agent types. Each has a distinct role — understanding boundaries prevents misrouting. Definitions live at `.claude/agents/{role}.md` (symlinked to `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/agents/{role}.md`).
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:324:| `manager` | Session chief — orchestration, user discussion, decision-making | The root session agent. Not Task-spawnable; this is the behavioral spec for the main agent. | Opus |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:325:| `leader` | PI/PM — research, ideation direction, planning decomposition | Ideation / Preparation / Research / Planning sub-phases. Single leader per dispatch. Writes artifacts; never implements code. | Opus |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:326:| `executor` | Implementation — code, edits, docs within scope | Execution phase. Reads brief + research, implements within scope boundary, returns one of 4 statuses with verification evidence. | Sonnet |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:327:| `evaluator` | Adversarial assessor — artifacts + process docs | Evaluation sub-phase (mandatory after Execution; optional after Ideation / Planning). Spawn exactly 2 in parallel — one per system (Claude + Codex). Each handles all 7 perspectives + Overall sequentially; cross-system divergence is the anti-groupthink signal. | Opus |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:328:| `assistant` | Lightweight support — references, lookups, codebase exploration | Narrow factual / read-only support; can parallelize. Read-only tool surface. | Sonnet |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:334:After each subagent returns, the manager extracts the delegation prompt and final result from the JSONL transcript and records them in session memory. Subagents do not need subtask doc instructions in their delegation prompt — their final response is the record.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/rules.md:28:Examples: `docs-cleanup-parallelism.md`, `evaluator-read-only-boundary.md`.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/reviews.md:16:`reviews/` is **not** a place for excerpted evaluator findings or curated highlights. The bar is **activity-shaped**: a review/audit/evaluation took place, and `reviews/` holds the document representing that activity.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/reviews.md:54:Carries the [shared base frontmatter](../rules.md#21-shared-base-every-memory-file) plus the reviews-type extensions (`verdict`, `review_kind`, `subject`). Reviews are project-only and append-only (base `status` stays `active`).
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/reviews.md:86:{The review's output — the substantive findings. Each finding with severity / confidence / evidence / proposed remediation. For evaluator-driven reviews, this section mirrors the structure of evaluation/SKILL.md's finding metadata. For human-authored reviews, the same fields apply but the form is narrative.}
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/references.md:18:- During **Ideation Sub-step C (Research)** when the leader surfaces a useful external source.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/references.md:19:- During any loop's MEMORIZATION when an evaluator's `general` finding contains a citable external pattern.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md:19:- During any loop's MEMORIZATION when an evaluator finding has `disposition: deferred` — the finding stages at `staging/decisions/{slug}.md` with `disposition: deferred` frontmatter; Wrap-up reads that flag and promotes the deferred decision into a backlog entry stamped from this template at `features/{feature-name}/backlogs/{slug}.md` or `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/backlogs/{slug}.md` per the deferred finding's scope.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md:71:{Optional — a one-paragraph sketch of how this might be tackled, drawing on the originating session's research. Helps the future session start faster.}
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md:80:- **Picked up** when a future session chooses this item as its workflow scope: the future session's manager reads this file and sets it as the session's `task` (or `feature`) in `session.json`
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md:85:A backlog file that has not been picked up in months and has no clear "when to pick up" trigger is dead weight. During wrap-up, the assistant flags stale backlogs to the user for explicit decision: keep, archive (move to `archive/backlogs/`), or drop (move to `archive/backlogs/` with `archive_reason: dropped`). Deletion is never an option — no-delete is a hard invariant.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/plans.md:67:| 1 | {Narrow, unambiguous sub-task} | — | {test / manual / metric / demo} | executor |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/plans.md:68:| 2 | {...} | #1 | ... | executor |
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/plans.md:83:When execution surfaces a need to change the plan (a sub-task was harder than expected, an ordering needed to flip), the assistant writes a new plan document at `{new-date}-{slug}.md` with `supersedes: {old-slug}` rather than editing in place — the version lives in frontmatter, never in the slug (no `-v2` suffix; [`rules.md` § 1.3](../rules.md) anti-pattern #6). The superseded plan is never deleted — at Wrap-up, it is moved (`git mv`) to `archive/plans/{date}-{slug}.md` per the move-on-terminal model. The active `plans/` directory then shows only live plans.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/templates/plans.md:87:Sub-tasks must be narrow enough that scope is unambiguous to a single executor agent. If a sub-task description starts with "and then" or "while doing this also", split it.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:3:description: How the manager constructs delegation prompts and hands off work to specialist subagents. Per-role templates, deterministic load directives, anti-pattern callouts, status contracts, and model selection.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:9:How the manager passes work to spawned subagents. The goal is **deterministic delegation** — the manager fills the same template the same way every time, the subagent loads the same things in the same order every time, nothing is left to inference.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:11:Sub-document of the `orchestration` skill. Loaded whenever the manager is about to call the `Agent` tool.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:23:A fresh subagent has no exposure to the manager's session — no transcript, no chain of thought, no skills the manager loaded earlier. The manager builds the context bundle inline. The subagent never reads the manager's mind.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:35:Every spawned agent reports with an explicit status enum at the end of its response. The enum is the last thing the subagent reads in the prompt before producing output (recency bias). The manager parses the status line first and dispatches deterministically.
/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/delegation/SKILL.md:39:MEMORIZATION is a specialized sub-phase with its own memory-tier boundaries, staging rules, and idempotency contract. A fresh subagent dispatched to run MEMORIZATION cannot operate correctly without loading `memorization/SKILL.md`. This is a hard gate: a delegation prompt that omits `memorization/SKILL.md` from the Skills tier when the sub-phase is MEMORIZATION is a malformed prompt — the manager must add it before dispatching.
